{"entities":"[{\"text\": \"Cerebral hemorrhage\", \"id\": \"D002543\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"phenylpropanolamine\", \"id\": \"D010665\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"caffeine\", \"id\": \"D002110\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"Phenylpropanolamine\", \"id\": \"D010665\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"PPA\", \"id\": \"D010665\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"stroke\", \"id\": \"D020521\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"caffeine\", \"id\": \"D002110\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"PPA\", \"id\": \"D010665\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"caffeine\", \"id\": \"D002110\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"stroke\", \"id\": \"D020521\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"hypertensive\", \"id\": \"D006973\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"hypertensive\", \"id\": \"D006973\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"PPA\", \"id\": \"D010665\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"caffeine\", \"id\": \"D002110\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"hypertension\", \"id\": \"D006973\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"hypertensive\", \"id\": \"D006973\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"PPA\", \"id\": \"D010665\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"caffeine\", \"id\": \"D002110\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"cerebral hemorrhage\", \"id\": \"D002543\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"hypertensive\", \"id\": \"D006973\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}]","filtered_entities":[{"text":"Cerebral hemorrhage","id":"D002543","label":"Disease"},{"text":"phenylpropanolamine","id":"D010665","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"caffeine","id":"D002110","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"stroke","id":"D020521","label":"Disease"},{"text":"hypertensive","id":"D006973","label":"Disease"}],"head":"caffeine","head_id":"D002110","pairs":[{"head":"phenylpropanolamine","tail":"Cerebral hemorrhage","head_id":"D010665","tail_id":"D002543"},{"head":"phenylpropanolamine","tail":"stroke","head_id":"D010665","tail_id":"D020521"},{"head":"phenylpropanolamine","tail":"hypertensive","head_id":"D010665","tail_id":"D006973"},{"head":"caffeine","tail":"Cerebral hemorrhage","head_id":"D002110","tail_id":"D002543"},{"head":"caffeine","tail":"stroke","head_id":"D002110","tail_id":"D020521"},{"head":"caffeine","tail":"hypertensive","head_id":"D002110","tail_id":"D006973"}],"relations":["D010665 | D002543","D010665 | D020521","D010665 | D006973","D002110 | D002543","D002110 | D020521","D002110 | D006973"],"result":"$","tail":"hypertensive","tail_id":"D006973","text":"Cerebral hemorrhage associated with phenylpropanolamine in combination with caffeine. Phenylpropanolamine (PPA) is a drug that has been associated with serious side effects including stroke. It is often combined with caffeine in diet preparations and \"look-alike\" pills. In order to determine if PPA/caffeine can lead to stroke in normotensive and/or hypertensive rats, we administered the combination in six times the allowed human dose calculated on a per weight basis for the rats two times per day for five days. Subarachnoid and cerebral hemorrhage was noted in 18% of the hypertensive rats. A single PPA/caffeine administration (same dose) lead to acute hypertension in both the normotensive and hypertensive animals. These results suggest that PPA/caffeine can lead to cerebral hemorrhage in previously hypertensive animals when administered in greater than the allowed dosage. An acute elevation in blood pressure may be a contributing factor.","metrics":{"precision":0.8333333333333334,"recall":0.7142857142857143,"f1":0.7692307692307693,"rel_tp":5,"rel_fp":1,"rel_fn":2}}